# TT.ESCALATION_INTERFACE.escalate_isp_outage_to_os (S-ESC-015..019) called directly for four
# ISP-outage events: (a) event without host/company -> the TICKET's host and company are used
# (NVL / COALESCE fallbacks), (b) event with its own host whose service company has a NULL short
# name -> 'Company: ' survives (S-ESC-018 NULL concatenation), (c) event with its own company ->
# the event's company wins over the ticket's, (d) no host on either the event or the ticket ->
# NO_DATA_FOUND arm: logged, no ticket created (S-ESC-016); plus a nonexistent event id. Each
# successful call opens a NEW hidden trouble ticket (type 1, no host, no company, no contact,
# service component 27) through TT.TICKET_INTERFACE.newticket_new with a 30005 event whose texts
# name the ORIGINAL ticket id and the original event's date; the original tickets stay untouched.
#
# The new tickets' ids are sequence-generated: they are selected by subject and told apart by the
# 30005 event's details_public, never by id.
#
# ORA_USER=system: fixtures insert into stop.company, mss.host, mss.service, mss.host2service.
ORA_USER=system
COMMITS=no
COMPARE_MSG=no
DESCRIPTION=escalate_isp_outage_to_os: host/company fallback chain (ticket host, event host, event company, NULL short), no-host -> logged no-op, nonexistent event; new hidden ticket + 30005 event texts naming the original ticket
